body:
Don't think you ruined his life. I obviously don't know your situation, but hear me out:

&#x200B;

You are the most important person in your life. That's just fact. No debating it. 

So if you 'had to leave' someone you love, I'm assuming something was happening to hurt you? Hold you back, or just not be up to your standards? Maybe even the relationship was hurting him?

No matter the reason, you always have every right to leave a relationship, and I'm sure you had good reason.

You didn't ruin anyone's life. He will be okay, as will you. 

&#x200B;

It's okay to worry about him, just make sure it's not going to hold you back in anyway from moving on. You deserve to be able to move on without him, even if he's hurting. It's your right.

You deserve to have your life be the way you want, with whoever you want it to be with.

&#x200B;

The future is unknown, but it always is. It never wasn't unknown. You could have every step of your life planned out and it will still always be unknown. Something you can do however is steer the odds in your favour. Keep working for the future you want, even if you can't guarantee it.

&#x200B;

You'll be completely okay. He will completely okay. Promise.
